  "summary": "Rewrote Act II Chapter 13 of Walk This Way (Draft 3.1) on branch draft-3.1-scalpel-hose as subagent 1 of 4. Converted the over-written 2,148-word Maxanne booth chapter into a 1,507-word first-person-present rewrite matching the Ch 8 DJ cadence: bourbon in a paper cup, ON AIR blinking, Bruins-hoodie engineer, the Maxell demo on the console, the Pink Floyd LP not yet dropped. Cut every 'machinery of division' speech, the 'Division always wins' sermon, and the 'aged bones' telling; corrected the 2024->2009 date and the obssesed/mighy/thirty-ears/cement-floors typos. Wove in Neighborhoods-as-private-benchmark, Mike Gordon/L-S single-line atmosphere, Lennon's Springsteen warning, and reserved 'crash the silence' for final broadcast. Preserved the earned money sentences ('hollow bones', 'paragraph and a misspelled last name') and added the Route 20 geography image and the turntable-vs-cassette decision beat. End pivots to the wooden bridge over Hop Brook, October 1978, late afternoon, oak leaves in the water — teeing up Ch 14. Output at /workspace/Draft_3/scalpel_hose_rewrites/ch13_rewrite.txt.",
  "current_status": "Ch 13 Scalpel & Hose rewrite complete and on disk. Word count 1,507 (in 1,500-1,900 band). POV, tense, weave-ins, and Ch 14 handoff all aligned to _SUBAGENT_BRIEF.md and DECISIONS_LOCKED.md. Super Agent can integrate; remaining three subagents unblocked for their chapters."
